	(text "3V3 INA219 current/voltage monitor - shunt 3V3_OUT -> 3V3, I2C addr 0x41"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 92.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2))
			(justify left bottom))
		(uuid "bc278ee4-f94a-5fd5-a740-2d6367134b4a"))
	(text "3.3 V Silent Switcher buck (LT80602): 5V0 -> 3V3_OUT, forced-continuous at a fixed ~506 kHz"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 156.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2))
			(justify left bottom))
		(uuid "6274dcad-b59d-5788-bea4-d227a3a3b555"))
	(text "Power sheet notes\n- CHANGE: the buck now runs from 5V0 (after the 5 V shunt) so the 5 V INA219 measures\n  the whole module input. In the Altium drawing the buck tapped 5V_BUS ahead of the shunt.\n- 5V0 also feeds the QPL9547 LNA (its recommended supply is 3.15-5.25 V, 5 V typ).\n- CHANGE: shunts 5 mOhm -> 50 mOhm. Expected 3V3 load ~0.45 A (LMX2582 ~0.25 A,\n  CC2595 ~0.1 A, nRF52840 + misc), so 5 mOhm only used 1/16th of the ADC range.\n- INA219 addresses: 5V monitor 0x40 (A0=A1=GND), 3V3 monitor 0x41 (A0=VS).\n- FIX: FB divider 681k/220k -> 634k/200k (ADI: RFB-BOT <= 205k). Vout = 0.8 x (1+634/200)\n  = 3.34 V, leaving headroom for shunt + bead drops to the LMX2582 (3.15 V min).\n- RT 37.4k -> fSW ~506 kHz (ADI eq. 2); L = 0.75 x Vout/fSW = 4.9 uH -> 5.6 uH;\n  CBST 1 uF (ADI Table 7). Pinout verified against ADI datasheet Rev 2, Table 3.\n- LT80602 exposed pad is internally VIN: it connects to 5V0, NOT GND.\n- CHANGE: SYNC/MODE GND (Burst) -> INTVCC (forced continuous): fixed 506 kHz keeps the\n  switching spurs at a known offset from the carrier; BST cap is 0.1 uF in FCM."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 440 20 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27))
			(justify left top))
		(uuid "a0cdab91-025a-5b44-aae9-e5032139f7ac"))
